CLINICAL AND DISORDER CONTENT
-----------------------------
content/registries/*.json, content/disorders/*.json, content/markers.json
and content/schema/*:

    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

All claims are original summaries carrying source IDs that resolve to
content/registries/sources.json. No text is copied verbatim from copyrighted
guidelines or reference works. DrugBank material is cited only; no raw
DrugBank records, affinity tables or Ki values are redistributed.

PRECISION AND INTENDED USE
-------------------------
Imaging-registered structures (globus pallidus internal/external split,
thalamic nuclei groups, subthalamic nucleus, substantia nigra, nucleus
accumbens, amygdala functional groups, hypothalamus zones, white-matter
tracts) remain CC BY-SA 4.0. They are approximate (about 7 mm resolution),
are educational, and are not for clinical use. Mapping precision is labelled
per structure as exact, proxy or schematic. See README.md for per-atlas
credits and the public/brain-atlas/models/manifest.json note.

THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
----------------------
Three.js, Draco, Vite and the anatomy data sources are third-party works
under their own licences. They are enumerated in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and
DATA_LICENSES.md.

A note on a past inconsistency: an earlier revision of DATA_LICENSES.md
described the code as MIT. No MIT licence file or SPDX header ever existed in
this repository, and the Apache 2.0 notice above is the operative grant. The
discrepancy is recorded in DATA_LICENSES.md.
